93 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107465 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107465 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186107468 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107465 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e907c4ba-8343-5fdd-abfe-8b39f70e8112" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107466 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107466 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107466 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9ec68db2-863b-55ad-8b69-eefdfc5401ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107467 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107467 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107467 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "af56ea0b-013c-519d-a19e-24c5eecb6eb9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107468 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107468 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107468 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "269504ce-2a6a-5ccd-9cf4-5b401742671b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107469 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107469 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107469 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5b210728-6a80-5b8f-97a2-05caf904c89a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107470 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107470 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107470 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7ddee60b-d64d-5874-a34e-03b6baff8ee0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110295 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10748" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110295 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/2f/2f6d703c604c780da8c97a012b94e75f06a55aa8b6e706a1097dc33ff193e88c.png)\n\nGiven the picture shown above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The points $K$, $N$, and $Z$ are collinear\n\nII. The points $K$, $P$, and $J$ are collinear" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110295 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a042ba66-3567-5b06-84e6-344ad0043bbc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110295 #edb/ref 1074 "- Statement I is false. We can't draw a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/39/390f01ec8631f4c4eca0f391dd5b1c2f9e450e94d3bd992e6046c42dff0fc1e8.png)\n\n- Statement II is true. There is a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/d9/d9d250f402d238388931ec077d17afe65b248d245ae6333f9cb150c18288ccce.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110296 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10749" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110296 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the diagrams below shows three collinear points?\n\n![](images/c0/c0df27c96da9f9c285438faee93652f81362fe91a51dc28e02ec0e2e9ff42177.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110296 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "76902823-634d-5525-afc5-5f2a98cea481" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110296 #edb/ref 1074 "Three (or more) points are collinear if a straight line passes through all points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our diagrams in turn.\n\n- Diagram I shows three points that are *not* collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.\n\n![](images/49/4967d8325f8ed8415a8404286d29ff97eb65cd6926ed1ca27a943178aee1a3cc.png)\n\n- Diagram II shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](images/af/af746af6fba54f69570f5dcfa38fbbb4cffd290080cc45deec433bc5266aa75e.png)\n\n- Diagram III shows three points that are *not* collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.\n\n![](images/c0/c0d9d178c5be09aa7f6ad1927c6f8e930154cf077aabbd18a765820babd63069.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110674 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186110905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110674 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111394 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110674 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110674 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110674 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110674 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441212 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110674 #edb/ref 1039 "Determining Whether Points on Intersecting Lines Are Collinear" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110674 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110674 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "f67c3319-1153-51ed-a57a-f85c06c7e76c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110675 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110675 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186110928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110675 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186110929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110675 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110675 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110675 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110675 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441211 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110675 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Collinear Points on a Grid" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110675 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110296 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110675 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "9ef4e321-841e-5933-b5e4-ff7dab6c5275" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110859 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111613 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110859 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111614 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110859 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111615 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110859 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110859 #edb/ref 1045 "Collinear Points" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110859 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186111613 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110859 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110859 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110859 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "dc520173-74e8-57e7-ad6f-9e7a82ef78e1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110905 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186107321 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110905 #edb/ref 1069 "q-13445" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110905 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110905 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/36/36ea34524b2ca277e8061441492711d36c8065e765d519d85d4008da97c3f8b3.png)\n\nConsider the figure shown above. Which of the following triplets of points are collinear?\n\nI. $M,N,R$\n\nII. $P,S,T$\n\nIII. $O,P,S$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110905 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d5df118a-6629-591e-bac9-243a7536e271" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110905 #edb/ref 1074 "- $M,N,R$ are collinear since there is a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/b8/b8fae613772422b14fce2e2db0762f659599f0b17409223ec291802b5d760d9c.png)\n\n- $P,S,T$ are **not** collinear since we can't draw a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/85/85638c1466360f3e5285c34e84903824140b9e2fc72a0f029ab1ded170b64eb2.png)\n\n- $O,P,S$ are collinear since there is a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/4b/4b7ef30e306e3c7e70dadb1524e1f60a9ea01832215009ef2ea8344cb07e7297.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110929 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186107465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110929 #edb/ref 1069 "q-155503" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110929 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110929 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/bb/bb96a7692787ca6e055b41d4f1599b87baa1ea331544ea42235a7131343c76e3.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams above shows three collinear points?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110929 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4ea9e0d7-7c8f-5224-8f6f-e5c31c36ab4a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110929 #edb/ref 1074 "Three (or more) points are collinear if a straight line passes through all points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our diagrams in turn.\n\n- Diagram I shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](images/54/54735541d4dfc424fe186ddabe0c3f9d3cbd45a0dc7a1b8f4551cf8c5e5bc14f.png)\n\n- Diagram II shows three points that are *not* collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.\n\n![](images/f0/f00f882c97fd201178e54f29151a48a4f41d4108cf375104cc338e968c55761b.png)\n\n- Diagram III shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](images/6e/6e0c0320775d93364e32655d1e09081382078fa7e96fbe621a8c558f63dfcabb.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111613 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111615 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111613 #edb/ref 1061 40727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111613 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2afa6da4-491a-5a31-8b50-09bd210fc929" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111613 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111906 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111614 #edb/ref 1061 40728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111614 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "08fe2b06-8140-5116-be8c-f9a047f0e538" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111614 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110674 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111615 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111614 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111615 #edb/ref 1061 40731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111615 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f4bbacca-99b9-57fe-b9c5-a2075ef9663b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111615 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111906 #edb/ref 1064 "For any two distinct points, there is always one (and only one) line that passes through them.\n\nFor example, the line passing through the points $P$ and $Q$ is $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{PQ},$ while the line that passes through $A$ and $B$ is $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{AB}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/8c/8c79a551e7ced71de157ea292baa3d7f38afaca4ea76ee467fc4add1b28ed33f.png)\n\nHowever, given three or more points, there is not always a line that passes through all of them.\n\nFor example, for the three points $F, G,$ and $H$ below, it is impossible to draw a single straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/30/30361c0bd49e571e317746f2d88848626da52e5ddbcda8fe9b6f496e4aff6b69.png)\n\nHowever, it is *sometimes* possible to draw a line through three (or more) points. In such cases, we say that the points are **collinear**.\n\nFor example, the points $M,$ $N,$ and $O$ shown below are collinear since they all lie on the same line.\n\n![](images/bf/bf3de55518c21de30718b2d9fee7032139c89aa3a4a963b8346b457ceafbeada.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111906 #edb/ref 1065 6732 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111906 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "051ac95a-dc63-5270-a5fa-a498a36c8297" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111906 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441157 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441157 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441157 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "004b80fe-aa14-5965-b4ca-127d549ed72f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441158 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441158 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441158 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "02057e88-897b-5572-b38e-d69c819eeed3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441159 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441159 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441159 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "09c250ea-692c-547e-a705-4dc418eb0270" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441160 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441160 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441160 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0ad41565-a704-532b-bb33-f22b0b4d71bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441161 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441161 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 